azgor wrote:

> [10]: (a)pplying a stethoscope to a door should allow you to hear
> what's on the other side (such as shops or special rooms). --JoshJ

This is consistent with the TDTTOE philosophy and would be at least
marginally useful.  It should give the same message you would randomly
get anyway: "Your hear someone complaining about shoplifters", "You
hear the tones of courtly conversation", etc.

This would provide a way of knowing for sure whether you _really_ want
to kick down that door, or come back to it when you've found an
unlocking method.

Applying it to the door Rodney is behind could generate YAFM: "You hear
someone complaining about adventurers".

> [11]: Candy Bars should give you a ten turn speed boost --Cheapy|

And abuse Con, to balance that out.

> [14]: There should always be a guaranteed random instrument available
> before arriving at the castle. --aristotle73

I think this is generally a good idea, since there's currently no
guarantee'd way to enter the castle at all, which seems inconsistent
with the general philosophy of NetHack (everything else you need to win
is guarantee'd, except 7 candles, which are practically guarantee'd).

> [15]: Using a scroll of enchant weapon while wielding an iron chain
> should produce a chain whip. It should be similar to a bullwhip, but
> deal better damage (and actually hurt thick-skinned monsters).

It's a good idea, since there's currently almost no use at all for the
appropriate weapon skill.  Probably w)ielding a chain should be treated
as a (poor) whip-class weapon, and ?oEW should "upgrade" it to a "chain
whip".



